Subject: [PATCH 31/33] plugin: add runtime plugin persistence framework

Add framework support for persisting and restoring
plugin-owned runtime state across log manager restarts.

Plugin state is serialized into the JSON log entry
representation using the plugin interface name as the
persistence key. During log restoration, persisted plugin
state is reconstructed through the plugin framework using
factory-based deserialization.

This change adds:
- Plugin::serialize() persistence support
- PluginFactory::deserialize() restoration hook
- PluginManager::deserialize() reconstruction logic
- PluginService::deserialize() integration API
- Entry plugin accessors for persistence workflows
- Plugin state serialization in elog JSON entries
- Plugin state restoration during log manager startup
- Unit test coverage for plugin deserialization support

Individual plugins will add plugin-specific state
serialization and restoration support in follow-up changes.

Change-Id: I4fed96845638e4d950cab9a7ca15258abf7e19c4
Signed-off-by: Jayanth Othayoth <ojayanth@gmail.com>
